 "posture": "US equities are in a confirmed correction, not a garden-variety pullback: the S&P 500 fell 3.7% Friday to 6,910.39 (seventh straight down day, -8.6% on the week) with the VIX closing at 35.9 after touching 40 intraday, and breadth at 33.5/100 ('Weakening') caps the supported equity band at 40-60%. The Fed repricing toward a ~95-98% priced December hike and the reported SEC accounting probe at Nvidia keep the AI complex at the epicenter; even a record NVDA quarter ($115.8B revenue, Nov 17) no longer offsets multiple and governance risk. Crypto is independently risk-off (37.4/100, RISK_OFF) with only 11% of top alts above their 200DMA. Posture: hold the lower half of the 40-60% band, keep cash and utilities ballast, and wait for a volume-backed follow-through day before adding AI beta; Wednesday's October PCE is the week's pivot.",
 "sentiment": "Deeply risk-off: panic pricing with a VIX close of 35.9, only defensives (staples, healthcare) green, and roughly $1.5-2B of crypto liquidations in 24 hours. Fear, not fundamentals, is doing the selling — Nvidia's Nov 17 print was a record quarter.",
